# Keep the Vercel upload small (10MB request limit). Exclude the heavy
# non-source directories only — KEEP every workspace package.json/source so
# `pnpm install` can resolve the monorepo (build:demo = packages/shared + apps/web).

# Heavy non-source siblings (the actual >10MB offenders)
BIDCRM-design/
scratch_skills/
scratch_img/
.tmp/
.audit-screens/
.planning/
handoff/
.corepack/
.claude/
.codex/

# Build outputs / caches (also gitignored — belt-and-suspenders)
**/dist/
**/build/
**/.turbo/
**/.vite/
**/coverage/
**/playwright-report/
**/test-results/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Working artifacts not needed by the build
walteur-kit/
_relay/

# The Vercel project is the SPA ONLY — the API runs on Railway and the SPA calls
# it directly via VITE_API_URL. A root `api/` directory makes Vercel add an
# `@vercel/node` build, and its dependency tracing OOMs on this monorepo:
# `vercel build` dies with exit 134 after copying the static output but before
# writing `.vercel/output/config.json`, so the follow-up `--prebuilt` deploy
# fails with "Config file was not found". Keep the functions build out of it.
api/
